@@ -0,0 +1,165 @@
+---
+name: sigma-embed
+description: >-
+  Construct server-signed JWT embed URLs for Sigma workbooks, data models,
+  pages, and elements. Use whenever the user wants to embed Sigma content in
+  a host application, sign embed JWTs, set up SIGMA_BASE_URL / CLIENT_ID /
+  SECRET / EMAIL, choose between embed-user auto-provisioning and manual
+  user management, target a tagged document version, pass user attributes
+  or teams in the JWT, hide UI chrome with embed URL parameters, switch
+  connections per session, or restrict embedded data per user with
+  user attributes, teams, RLS, or CLS.
+---
+
+# Sigma Embed (Secure JWT)
+
+Construct a server-signed JWT and append it to the embed URL so the host application can render a Sigma workbook, page, element, data model, or report inside an iframe.
+
+**Requirements:** Node.js 18+ (the bundled script uses only `node:crypto` — no npm install). If you prefer the `jsonwebtoken` package, the example library snippet still applies. Sign the JWT **server-side**; never expose `SECRET` to the browser.
+
+## Embed Credentials
+
+Embed credentials are generated in Sigma at **Administration → Developer access → Create new**, with the **Embedding** scope checkbox enabled. The owner must be an Admin. You receive a `client_id` and a one-time `secret`; the secret cannot be retrieved again — revoke and regenerate if lost.
+
+The same Sigma client-credentials surface can also issue tokens for REST API calls (see the `sigma-api` skill). For embed signing, you only need the embed-scoped pair; for tag application or other API operations, generate a separate API-scoped credential.
+
+```sh
+# Server env only — never browser-facing.
+export SIGMA_BASE_URL="https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>-<workbookUrlId>"
+export SIGMA_CLIENT_ID="embed-client-id"
+export SIGMA_SECRET="embed-secret"
+export SIGMA_EMAIL="user@example.com"
+```
+
+The `SIGMA_BASE_URL` here is the **embed target URL** copied from Sigma's app — not the REST API host. URL formats per document type live in `reference/embed-url-format.md`.
+
+## Step 1 — Construct the JWT
+
+The JWT carries claims that identify and authorize the embed session. Required claims: `sub`, `jti`, `iat`, `exp`, and `kid` (in the header). Optional claims customize the embed user, restrict data, or switch behavior.
+
+### Preferred: bundled helper script
+
+`scripts/generate-embed-url.js` reads env vars and prints the signed URL to stdout. Useful for verifying credentials, exploring the URL shape, and ad-hoc debugging.
+
+- **Claude Code:** `node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/sigma-embed/scripts/generate-embed-url.js`
+- **Cursor / Codex / generic:** `node <repo-root>/skills/sigma-embed/scripts/generate-embed-url.js`
+
+| In (env) | Out (stdout) |
+|----------|--------------|
+| `SIGMA_BASE_URL`, `SIGMA_CLIENT_ID`, `SIGMA_SECRET`, `SIGMA_EMAIL` | A single signed embed URL |
+
+Optional env: `SIGMA_SESSION_LENGTH` (seconds, default 3600, max 2592000), `SIGMA_ACCOUNT_TYPE`, `SIGMA_TEAMS` (comma-separated), `SIGMA_USER_ATTRIBUTES` (JSON object).
+
+### Reference implementation (Node.js, no npm deps)
+
+```js
+import { createHmac, randomUUID } from 'node:crypto';
+
+function buildEmbedUrl({ baseUrl, clientId, secret, email, sessionLength = 3600, extraClaims = {} }) {
+  const b64 = (obj) => Buffer.from(JSON.stringify(obj)).toString('base64url');
+  const now = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);
+  const header = { alg: 'HS256', typ: 'JWT', kid: clientId };
+  const payload = {
+    sub: email,
+    iss: clientId,
+    jti: randomUUID(),
+    iat: now,
+    exp: now + Math.min(sessionLength, 2592000),
+    ...extraClaims,
+  };
+  const unsigned = `${b64(header)}.${b64(payload)}`;
+  const sig = createHmac('sha256', secret).update(unsigned).digest('base64url');
+  const token = `${unsigned}.${sig}`;
+  return `${baseUrl}?:jwt=${encodeURIComponent(token)}&:embed=true`;
+}
+```
+
+### Reference implementation (Node.js, with `jsonwebtoken`)
+
+Matches the example in Sigma's official documentation.
+
+```js
+const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
+const { v4: uuid } = require('uuid');
+
+const token = jwt.sign(
+  {
+    sub: process.env.SIGMA_EMAIL,
+    iss: process.env.SIGMA_CLIENT_ID,
+    jti: uuid(),
+    iat: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000),
+    exp: Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) + 3600,
+  },
+  process.env.SIGMA_SECRET,
+  { algorithm: 'HS256', keyid: process.env.SIGMA_CLIENT_ID }
+);
+const signedUrl = `${process.env.SIGMA_BASE_URL}?:jwt=${encodeURIComponent(token)}&:embed=true`;
+```
+
+For the complete claims catalog (`account_type`, `teams`, `user_attributes`, `oauth_token`, `eval_connection_id`, `tenant`, `ver`, `aud`, etc.) and when to use each, load `reference/jwt-claims.md`.
+
+## Step 2 — Choose the Embed URL Target
+
+The base URL changes shape depending on what is being embedded — a whole workbook, a specific page, a single element, a data model, or a tagged version of any of these. Tag-targeting is done with a `/tag/<tagName>` path segment inserted before the query string.
+
+Load `reference/embed-url-format.md` for the supported document-type URL formats, the tagged-version format, and how to pull IDs from the REST API when copy-pasting from the app isn't an option.
+
+## Step 3 — Manage Who Can Access the Embed
+
+Sigma supports two access models:
+
+1. **Automatic embed-user creation (default).** Sigma creates an account from the `sub` (email) claim on first access. The `teams`, `account_type`, `first_name`, `last_name`, and `user_attributes` claims drive the auto-provisioned user's setup. Best for SaaS apps where the host application is the identity provider.
+2. **Manual user management.** Disable automatic creation in **Administration → Embeds → Settings**; provision users via IdP, the [Create a member](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/reference/createmember) endpoint, or the Sigma UI. Internal users **must not** receive `teams`, `account_type`, or `user_attributes` claims — those values are managed inside Sigma.
+
+> **Important:** JWT claims are per-user, not per-session. Use consistent claim values for the same embed user across sessions. Do not use claims to gate what the same user sees in different sessions — manage that at the user/team level in Sigma.
+
+Load `reference/managing-users.md` for the full provisioning workflow, team setup, account-type assignment, and folder/workspace grants.
+
+## Step 4 — Restrict Data Per User
+
+The standard ways to restrict data shown to an embedded user are:
+
+| Mechanism | How it works | When to use |
+|-----------|--------------|-------------|
+| **Row-level security (RLS)** | Configured in a data model / dataset / custom SQL. Filters rows by `current_user_attribute('Name')`, team, or user. | Per-user or per-tenant row filtering. |
+| **Column-level security (CLS)** | Configured on data model columns. Restricts visibility by team or user attribute. | Hide sensitive columns from specific teams. |
+| **Warehouse role switching** | A user attribute is bound to a connection's role; Sigma uses that role for the session's queries. | Per-tenant data isolation enforced at the warehouse (e.g., one Snowflake role per customer). |
+| **OAuth token pass-through** | `oauth_token` or `connection_oauth_tokens` JWT claim authenticates to the warehouse as the embed user. | Identity-aware data access using an existing IdP/OAuth setup. |
+| **Connection swap** | A version tag of the workbook is bound to a different connection (via `sourceMappingConfig` on `POST /v2/workbooks/tag`), or the `eval_connection_id` JWT claim points the session at a different connection. | Promote between environments (dev/staging/prod) or point a single embed at per-customer connections. |
+| **Sigma Tenants (Beta)** | Separate tenant organizations under a parent org; full data and user isolation, deploy content with source swap. | Strict multi-tenant SaaS where customer data, users, and connections must be fully isolated. |
+
+Load `reference/multi-tenancy.md` for the detailed patterns and code examples.
+
+## Step 5 — Customize the Embed UI
+
+Append query string parameters (in addition to `?:jwt=...&:embed=true`) to hide chrome, set themes, change language, enable responsive height, or pre-populate control values.
+
+Load `reference/url-parameters.md` for the supported interface parameters and the control-value parameter syntax.
+
+## Verifying an Embed
+
+1. Decode the JWT in [jwt.io](https://jwt.io/) and confirm `kid` matches the embed client ID and required claims are present.
+2. In the host page, inspect the iframe `src` and confirm it contains `?:jwt=` and `&:embed=true`.
+3. Confirm the embed secret never appears in any network request initiated from the browser.
+4. If the embed shows a permissions error, verify (a) the workbook is shared with a team the embed user is assigned to, and (b) the `sub` email is RFC-1035 compliant (no underscores or whitespace).
+
+## Security Notes
+
+- Never sign JWTs in browser code — the embed secret would be exposed.
+- Never log `SIGMA_SECRET` or return it in API responses.
+- Keep `exp - iat` ≤ 30 days; default to 1 hour for typical embed sessions.
+- Generate a fresh `jti` per session — Sigma uses it as the session identifier.
+- For OAuth-bearing claims (`oauth_token`, `connection_oauth_tokens`), encrypt the token with the embed secret per the [Sigma Node.js Embed SDK](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sigmacomputing/node-embed-sdk).
+- If the embed secret is compromised, revoke it in Sigma; all JWTs signed with the old secret stop working immediately.
+- Treat the signed embed URL itself as sensitive — log access carefully and avoid persisting it.
+
+## Reference Index
+
+| File | When to load |
+|------|--------------|
+| `reference/jwt-claims.md` | Authoring or troubleshooting the JWT payload — claim names, types, header-vs-payload placement, version differences. |
+| `reference/embed-url-format.md` | Constructing the base URL for a workbook, page, element, data model, report, or tagged version. |
+| `reference/url-parameters.md` | Hiding UI chrome (`:hide_menu`, `:hide_bookmarks`), themes, language, responsive height, control values. |
+| `reference/multi-tenancy.md` | Restricting data per user/tenant: user attributes, warehouse role switching, OAuth, RLS, CLS, connection swap, Sigma Tenants. |
+| `reference/managing-users.md` | Embed-user auto-creation vs. manual provisioning, teams, account types, folder/workspace grants. |
+| `reference/version-tags.md` | Tagging workbooks, embedding tagged versions, swapping sources with the tag, `POST /v2/workbooks/tag` payload shape. |
