+# Embed URL Format
+
+The "base URL" referenced throughout this skill is the **embed target URL** copied from Sigma's app — not the REST API host. The exact format depends on what is being embedded. Source: [Sigma: Create an embed API with JSON Web Tokens](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/create-an-embed-api-with-json-web-tokens).
+
+## Document-Type URL Structures
+
+Open the **published** version of the document in Sigma and copy the URL from the browser, or build it from API results.
+
+| Document type | URL structure |
+|---------------|---------------|
+| **Workbook** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>-<workbookUrlId>` |
+| **Page** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>-<workbookId>/page/<pageId>` |
+| **Element** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>-<workbookId>/element/<elementId>` |
+| **Data model** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/data-model/<dataModelName>-<dataModelUrlId>` |
+| **Report** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/report/<reportName>-<reportUrlId>` |
+| **Sigma Assistant** | `https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/ask` |
+
+## Tagged Document Versions
+
+To embed a tagged version of a workbook, data model, or report, append `/tag/<tagName>` **before** the query string:
+
+```
+https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>-<workbookUrlId>/tag/<tagName>
+https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/data-model/<dataModelName>-<dataModelUrlId>/tag/<tagName>
+```
+
+For public embeds the form is `/embed/<embedId>/tag/<tagName>`.
+
+Tag names containing spaces or special characters must be URL-encoded — e.g., `staging%20copy` for a tag named "Staging Copy".
+
+See `reference/version-tags.md` for the version-tag lifecycle and the tag-application API.
+
+## Getting IDs From the REST API
+
+When you can't copy a URL from the browser — e.g., embedding a page or element programmatically — pull the IDs from these endpoints:
+
+| What | Endpoint |
+|------|----------|
+| `workbookId`, workbook URL | `GET /v2/workbooks` (List workbooks) |
+| `pageId` | `GET /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/pages` |
+| `elementId` | `GET /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/pages/{pageId}/elements` |
+| `dataModelId`, data model URL | `GET /v2/dataModels` (List data models) |
+
+The API returns URLs in a slightly different format than the browser address bar:
+```
+https://app.sigmacomputing.com/<organizationSlug>/workbook/<workbookName>/<workbookId>
+```
+Both formats are accepted by the embed signer.
+
+## Final Signed URL Shape
+
+After signing the JWT and appending it:
+
+```
+<baseUrl>?:jwt=<URL-encoded JWT>&:embed=true
+```
+
+Or with a tag:
+```
+<baseUrl>/tag/<tagName>?:jwt=<URL-encoded JWT>&:embed=true
+```
+
+Additional URL parameters (`:hide_menu`, `:theme`, etc.) and control-value parameters are appended after `:embed=true` with `&` separators. See `reference/url-parameters.md`.
