@@ -0,0 +1,155 @@
+# Restricting Data Per User (Multi-Tenant Patterns)
+
+Six Sigma-documented mechanisms for showing different data to different embed users from the same workbook. None require duplicating workbooks per tenant. Source: [Sigma: Restrict access to data in embedded content](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/restrict-access-to-data-in-embedded-content).
+
+## 1. Row-Level Security (RLS)
+
+Configure RLS in the data model, dataset, or custom SQL. Rules reference user attributes, team membership, or specific users. At query time Sigma applies the filter based on the session's effective user.
+
+Setup:
+1. Define a user attribute (e.g. `CustomerId`) in Sigma admin.
+2. In the data model, add an RLS rule like `CUSTOMER_ID = current_user_attribute('CustomerId')`.
+3. Pass the user attribute via JWT (auto-created users) or assign it to teams in Sigma (internal users).
+
+```js
+// JWT payload (auto-created embed user)
+{
+  sub: 'user@customer-a.example',
+  user_attributes: { CustomerId: 'A' },
+}
+```
+
+## 2. Column-Level Security (CLS)
+
+Restrict column visibility on a data model based on team membership or user attributes. Configured in the data model, not the workbook.
+
+```js
+{
+  sub: 'finance@acme.example',
+  teams: ['Finance'],   // CLS rules grant column access by team
+}
+```
+
+## 3. Warehouse Role Switching (User Attribute → Connection Role)
+
+For supported data platforms (e.g. Snowflake with key-pair auth), bind a user attribute to a connection's role. Sigma uses the per-user role when issuing queries.
+
+Setup:
+1. In the warehouse, create one role per tenant with USAGE granted on that tenant's schema.
+2. In Sigma admin, create a `Role` user attribute (no default).
+3. On the Sigma connection, set **Role** to the `Role` user attribute.
+4. Pass the role value in the JWT (auto-created users) or assign to teams (internal users).
+
+```sql
+-- Snowflake
+GRANT USAGE ON CUSTOMER_DATA.ABC TO ROLE ABC;
+```
+
+```js
+// JWT payload
+{
+  user_attributes: { Role: 'ABC' },
+}
+```
+
+> Not compatible with OAuth-authenticated connections.
+
+## 4. OAuth Token Pass-Through
+
+Authenticate the warehouse query as the actual embed user. Two variants:
+
+| Use case | JWT claim | Notes |
+|----------|-----------|-------|
+| OAuth for both Sigma login and warehouse | `oauth_token` | Encrypt with embed secret. |
+| OAuth only for warehouse | `connection_oauth_tokens` | Per-connection map; keys are connection IDs, values are encrypted tokens. |
+
+Both require `ver: "1.1"` and token encryption per the [Sigma Node.js Embed SDK](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sigmacomputing/node-embed-sdk).
+
+```js
+{
+  ver: '1.1',
+  aud: 'sigmacomputing',
+  connection_oauth_tokens: {
+    '1a2b3456-c7d8-91ef-23g4-h56i7jkl8912': '<encrypted-token>',
+  },
+}
+```
+
+## 5. Connection Swap via Version Tag
+
+Bind a tagged workbook version to a different connection at tag-application time. Standard pattern for dev/staging/prod and for per-tenant deployments where each tenant has its own connection.
+
+Apply with `POST /v2/workbooks/tag` (requires API credentials, not embed credentials):
+
+```json
+{
+  "workbookId": "12345678910",
+  "tag": "customer-a",
+  "sourceMappingConfig": [{
+    "fromConnectionId": "<dev-connection-id>",
+    "toConnectionId":   "<customer-a-connection-id>",
+    "paths": [{
+      "fromPath": ["DEV_DB", "PUBLIC", "ORDERS"],
+      "toPath":   ["CUSTOMER_A_DB", "PUBLIC", "ORDERS"]
+    }]
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+Then embed the tagged URL: `<baseUrl>/tag/customer-a?:jwt=...&:embed=true`. See `reference/version-tags.md` for the complete tag API.
+
+## 6. Per-Session Connection Switch via `eval_connection_id`
+
+The `eval_connection_id` JWT claim overrides the workbook's default connection for that session only — no tag needed.
+
+```js
+{
+  eval_connection_id: '1a2b3456-c7d8-91ef-23g4-h56i7jkl8912',
+}
+```
+
+Trade-offs:
+- ✅ No version tag management required.
+- ❌ Not supported with OAuth-authenticated connections.
+- ❌ Not supported with write-back features (input tables, materialization, Python elements).
+
+Get connection IDs from `GET /v2/connections`.
+
+## 7. Sigma Tenants (Beta)
+
+Premium feature for true multi-org isolation. The parent organization provisions tenant orgs with their own users, connections, and settings; content deploys to tenants via deployment policies with automatic source swap.
+
+```js
+{
+  ver: '1.1',
+  aud: 'sigmacomputing',
+  tenant: '<tenant-org-uuid>',  // from GET /v2/tenants
+}
+```
+
+When to use:
+- Each customer's data, users, and connections must be **fully** isolated at the Sigma layer (not just at the row/column/role layer).
+- Compliance requires data sovereignty per tenant.
+- A managed-service-provider model where each customer is effectively a separate Sigma org.
+
+See [Sigma Tenants documentation](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/multitenancy-at-sigma).
+
+## Choosing an Approach
+
+| Need | Recommended mechanism |
+|------|----------------------|
+| Per-user row filtering inside shared tables | RLS with user attributes |
+| Hide columns from specific teams | CLS |
+| Each tenant's data lives in a separate warehouse schema, single connection | Warehouse role switching |
+| Per-customer warehouse connection | Connection swap via version tag, or `eval_connection_id` |
+| Identity passes through to the warehouse | OAuth claims |
+| Dev / staging / production lifecycle | Version tag + `sourceMappingConfig` |
+| Full per-tenant Sigma org isolation | Sigma Tenants |
+
+Mechanisms compose. For example, a single workbook can use warehouse role switching for query-time isolation **and** RLS for per-user row filtering **and** CLS for sensitive-column gating — all driven by user attributes carried in the JWT.
+
+## What This Skill Does **Not** Recommend
+
+- Maintaining one workbook per customer. Sigma's documented multi-tenant patterns route through user attributes, connections, and tags — not document duplication.
+- Mutating a single workbook's spec on each embed request to customize what a customer sees. The mechanisms above (RLS, CLS, warehouse role switching, connection swap, OAuth) deliver per-customer views without spec mutation and without the concurrency hazards of mutate-then-render.
+- Using JWT claims to gate what the same user sees in different sessions. Claims are per-user; per-session gating belongs in the host application's filtering layer (e.g., URL control values).
