+# Embed URL Parameters
+
+URL query-string parameters that customize the embed in addition to the JWT. Append after `?:jwt=...&:embed=true` with `&` separators. Source: [Sigma: Embed URL parameters](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/embed-url-parameters).
+
+## Usage Notes
+
+- Values must be URL-encoded. See [URL encoding reference for parameters](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/special-characters-for-url-parameters).
+- For comma-separated multi-values, **do not** encode the commas — pass `value1,value2`, not `value1%2Cvalue2`.
+- Parameter values are case-sensitive (`true`, not `True`).
+
+## Interface Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Description |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| `:hide_bookmarks` | When `true`, hides saved views from the embed menu. |
+| `:hide_element_interactions` | When `true`, hides the element toolbar (filter menu, More menu, etc.). |
+| `:hide_explore_toggle` | When `true`, hides the explore toggle from the embed menu. |
+| `:hide_folder_navigation` | When `true`, hides the folder navigation. |
+| `:hide_menu` | When `true`, hides the embed menu in saved workbooks. Only takes effect when `:menu_position` is `top` or `bottom`. |
+| `:hide_save_as` | When `true`, hides the **Save As** button without hiding page navigation. |
+| `:hide_schedule` | When `true`, hides the schedule-export menu option. Does **not** prevent users from scheduling — use the **Schedule export** account-type permission for enforcement. |
+| `:hide_send` | When `true`, hides the download menu option. Does **not** prevent downloads — use the **Download** account-type permission for enforcement. (PDF page / PNG element downloads are never hidden by this flag.) |
+| `:hide_tooltip` | When `true`, hides chart mark tooltips. |
+| `:lng` | Locale for Sigma UI text. Applies any matching custom translations. |
+| `:lng_variant` | Custom translation variant. Must be used with `:lng`. |
+| `:menu_position` | `top`, `bottom`, or `none` (default `none`). |
+| `:responsive_height` | When `true`, enables the JS event [`workbook:pageheight:onchange`](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/outbound-event-reference#workbookpageheightonchange) for responsive iframe sizing. Set `false` for workbook edit URLs (those containing `/edit`). |
+| `:theme` | Workbook theme by name — `Light`, `Dark`, `Surface`, or any custom theme. Case-sensitive. |
+
+## Control Values
+
+Pre-populate workbook control values by adding `<controlId>=<value>` query parameters. Details: [Set control values in a URL using query string parameters](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/workbook-control-values-in-the-url).
+
+Example: a list control whose `controlId` is `region` defaulting to `West`:
+```
+&region=West
+```
+
+Multi-value list controls accept comma-separated values:
+```
+&region=West,East
+```
+
+## Example Full URL
+
+```
+https://app.sigmacomputing.com/acme/workbook/Sales-1abc2def3ghi
+  ?:jwt=<token>
+  &:embed=true
+  &:hide_folder_navigation=true
+  &:menu_position=bottom
+  &:theme=Dark
+  &:responsive_height=true
+  &region=West
+```
+
+(Line-broken here for readability — in practice send as a single line.)
