+# Version Tags for Embeds
+
+Version tags freeze a specific document version under a named handle (e.g. `staging`, `production`, `region-east`) and create an immutable read-only view that survives further edits to the source document. Embeds can target a tag instead of the live published version. Source: [Sigma: Add version tags to workbooks and data models](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/add-version-tags-to-workbooks-and-data-models).
+
+## Documented Use Cases
+
+| Pattern | Tag names |
+|---------|-----------|
+| Promotion lifecycle | `dev` → `staging` → `production` |
+| Region or team isolation | `region-east`, `region-west` |
+| Snapshot for audit / point-in-time review | `audit-2026-Q1` |
+| Connection swap per environment or tenant | `prod-snowflake`, `customer-a-snowflake` |
+
+Tag names with spaces or special characters must be URL-encoded in the embed URL — `staging%20copy` for `"Staging Copy"`.
+
+## Embedding a Tagged Version
+
+URL form (insert `/tag/<tagName>` before the query string):
+
+```
+<baseWorkbookUrl>/tag/<tagName>?:jwt=<token>&:embed=true
+<baseDataModelUrl>/tag/<tagName>?:jwt=<token>&:embed=true
+```
+
+For public embeds: `/embed/<embedId>/tag/<tagName>`.
+
+The JWT signing logic is identical — only the URL changes.
+
+## Applying a Tag via the REST API
+
+Endpoint: `POST /v2/workbooks/tag` (or `POST /v2/dataModels/tag` for data models). Requires API credentials with appropriate scopes — use the `sigma-api` skill to obtain a bearer token.
+
+### Minimal request
+
+```json
+{
+  "workbookId": "12345678910",
+  "tag": "production"
+}
+```
+
+### With source swap (e.g. promoting from dev to prod warehouse)
+
+```json
+{
+  "workbookId": "12345678910",
+  "tag": "production",
+  "workbookVersion": 4,
+  "sourceMappingConfig": [{
+    "fromConnectionId": "<dev-connection-id>",
+    "toConnectionId":   "<prod-connection-id>",
+    "paths": [{
+      "fromPath": ["DEV_DB", "WEATHER", "DAILY_14_TOTAL"],
+      "toPath":   ["PROD_DB", "WEATHER", "DAILY_16_TOTAL"]
+    }]
+  }],
+  "isDefault": true
+}
+```
+
+### With data-model tag binding
+
+If the workbook reads from a data model, you usually want the tagged workbook to read from a tagged version of the data model. Tag the data model first (`POST /v2/dataModels/tag`), then bind:
+
+```json
+{
+  "workbookId": "12345678910",
+  "tag": "production",
+  "dataModelSourceTaggedVersions": [{
+    "dataModelId":      "<data-model-id>",
+    "fromVersionTagId": null,
+    "toVersionTagId":   "<data-model-prod-tag-id>"
+  }]
+}
+```
+
+`fromVersionTagId: null` means "currently reading from the latest published data model". `toVersionTagId: null` means "swap to the latest published data model" (rather than a tagged version). Get `versionTagId` values from `GET /v2/dataModels` and `GET /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/sources`.
+
+### Response
+
+```json
+{
+  "versionTagId": "<tag-id>",
+  "taggedWorkbookId": "12345678910",
+  "taggedWorkbookVersion": 4
+}
+```
+
+## Tag Lifecycle
+
+| Operation | Endpoint / UI |
+|-----------|---------------|
+| Create a tag definition (must exist before it can be applied) | `POST /v2/tags` or UI: **Administration → Tags** |
+| Apply a tag to a workbook version | `POST /v2/workbooks/tag` |
+| List tags on a workbook | `GET /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/tags` |
+| Remove a tag from a workbook | `DELETE /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/tags/{tagId}` |
+| Delete a tag definition | `DELETE /v2/tags/{tagId}` |
+| Duplicate a tagged workbook | `POST /v2/workbooks/{workbookId}/tag/{versionTag}/copy` |
+
+## Updating a Tagged Version
+
+Tags themselves are immutable in the sense that they bind to a specific workbook version. To "update" a tagged version:
+
+1. Restore the tagged version as a draft (UI: **Versions → Version history → Restore version as draft**).
+2. Make changes; publish.
+3. Apply the same tag to the new published version.
+
+The previous version retains a grayed-out reference to the tag in version history. **Do not remove the tag from the old version** — anyone who only had access via the tag would lose access. Re-applying the tag to a new version preserves sharing.
+
+## User Requirements
+
+To apply tags:
+- **Can Edit** permission on the document.
+- Account type with the **Apply Tag** permission.
+- Document-type-specific permission: **Create, edit, and publish workbooks** (or reports, or data models).
+
+Protected tags require additional approval — see [Create and manage version tags](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/create-and-manage-version-tags).
+
+## Materialization Caveat
+
+Tagged document versions interact with materialization differently:
+- **Materialized dataset:** the tagged workbook uses a **copy** of the dataset, not the materialized version.
+- **Materialized data model:** the materialized version **is** used.
+- **Tagged data model:** if the tagged data model is materialized, that materialized version is used.
+
+See [About materialization](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/sigma-computing/docs/materialization).
